The defect: the split carves first and asks the ceiling second. It reads as a reordering with no
effect, since both checks still run, but a split the ceiling refuses has already advanced the
parent's watermark and raised its child count.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(run.snapshots() == before, "a refusal moved something")`,
on a split refused at the region ceiling.

